CodexMeter is an independent, unofficial application powered by CodexBar.

Windows v0.1.3 packages include the Win-CodexBar 0.45.2 standalone console CLI
so users do not need to install the Win-CodexBar desktop application. The exact
binary is pinned and verified with SHA-256 at build time and before execution.
Its MIT license is included at:

  ThirdPartyLicenses/Win-CodexBar-LICENSE.txt

and beside the Windows executable as:

  Win-CodexBar-LICENSE.txt

Win-CodexBar:
  https://github.com/nesszer/Win-CodexBar
  Licensed under the MIT License:
  https://github.com/nesszer/Win-CodexBar/blob/main/LICENSE

macOS packages include the upstream CodexBar CLI and its license at:

  ThirdPartyLicenses/CodexBar-LICENSE.txt

and inside the application bundle at:

  CodexMeter.app/Contents/Resources/ThirdPartyLicenses/

CodexBar:
  https://github.com/steipete/CodexBar
  Copyright (c) 2025 Peter Steinberger
  Licensed under the MIT License:
  https://github.com/steipete/CodexBar/blob/main/LICENSE

The bundled CodexBar CLI also incorporates these pinned open-source
dependencies. Their complete license and notice files are included in the
application bundle:

  Commander 0.2.2
  https://github.com/steipete/Commander

  SweetCookieKit 0.4.1
  https://github.com/steipete/SweetCookieKit

  Swift Crypto 3.15.1
  https://github.com/apple/swift-crypto

  SwiftLog 1.13.2
  https://github.com/apple/swift-log

  Swift ASN.1 1.7.1
  https://github.com/apple/swift-asn1

The edge docking interaction was informed by SideTerminal's compact
edge-reveal approach. CodexMeter contains an independent AppKit implementation
and does not redistribute SideTerminal source code.

